Data Preparation
The first step involved cleaning and organizing the raw data to ensure accuracy and consistency. This included:
Removing duplicate records
Handling NULL values appropriately
Standardizing formats (dates, text fields, categories)
Correcting data inconsistencies
Filtering out unusable or corrupted entries


Normalizing
After cleaning, the dataset was normalized to improve structure and consistency.
This involved standardizing column names, aligning data formats, and ensuring categories followed a uniform structure.


Data Querying
All analysis and transformation queries were executed using Snowflake, including filtering, aggregations, joins, and creating calculated fields to support further insights and reporting.
